.TH VECTOR 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Value Types"
.SH NAME
vector \- built-in mathematical vector value type methods
.SH DESCRIPTION
Vectors in y-- are specialized arrays for numeric values (ints and floats)
designed to support linear algebra operations.
.SH "PROPERTIES"
.TP
\fBdimension()\fR -> int()
Returns the dimensionality (number of elements) of the vector.
.TP
\fBmagnitude()\fR -> float()
Calculates and returns the Euclidean magnitude (length) of the vector.
.TP
\fBunitVec()\fR -> vector()
Returns a normalized copy of the vector (scaled so its magnitude is exactly 1). Throws MathError if the vector is the zero vector.
.SH "LINEAR ALGEBRA"
.TP
\fBdot(other_vec)\fR -> int()|float()
Returns the dot product (scalar product) of this vector and \fBother_vec\fR. Throws ValueError if dimensions do not match.
.TP
\fBcross(other_vec)\fR -> vector()
Returns the cross product of this vector and \fBother_vec\fR. Only defined for vectors of dimension 2 or 3. Throws ValueError otherwise.
.TP
\fBprojectOnto(other_vec)\fR -> vector()
Calculates the vector projection of this vector onto \fBother_vec\fR. Throws MathError if \fBother_vec\fR is the zero vector.
.SH "MANIPULATION"
.TP
\fBvector_reversal()\fR -> vector()
Reverses the elements of the vector in place.
.TP
\fBexpand(n)\fR -> vector()
Increases the dimensionality of the vector by appending \fBn\fR zeroes to the end.
.TP
\fBshrink(n)\fR -> vector()
Decreases the dimensionality of the vector by popping \fBn\fR elements from the end. Throws ValueError if the result would have a dimension less than 1.
.SH "FUNCTIONAL METHODS"
.TP
\fBAll_Of / Any_Of / None_Of / One_Of (lambda)\fR -> bool()
.TP
\fBselect / reject (lambda)\fR -> vector()|list()
Filters the vector. If the resulting elements are all numeric, returns a vector. Otherwise, falls back to a list.
.TP
\fBmap(lambda)\fR -> vector()|list()
Maps the elements. If the lambda returns all numeric values, returns a vector, otherwise a list.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Math(3), list(3)
